t2-touchid bridges the Touch ID sensor of Apple T2 Macs (2018-2020 Intel
MacBook Pro, MacBook Air, Mac mini, iMac Pro) to fprintd, so that login,
sudo and screen lockers can accept a finger through stock fprintd and
pam_fprintd.

The sensor belongs to the T2's Secure Enclave and is reachable only over
IPv6 link-local on the T2's internal USB CDC-NCM link (cdce on USB
05ac:8233). The bridge speaks BiometricKit to bridgeOS there and reports
the Secure Enclave's verdicts through libfprint's virtual storage device.
It never enrolls: fingers are enrolled under macOS, and the Secure Enclave
answers with an empty inventory until macOS has unlocked it once since the
T2 last powered on.

